        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0790" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v24/pg742"/>

                <head>425. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="1" xml:id="d425-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1964-08-06">August 6, 1964</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Meeting of 303 Committee on 6 August 1964</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Angola paper was set aside for the time being.<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d425-f2"/>
                    </item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>] paper was set aside for the time being.<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d425-f3"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <pb facs="0791" n="743" xml:id="pg743"/>
                <p>Note: The reason for this was that McCone
                    stated that in view of the confusion in the Congo, it was probably good judgment
                    to place the Roberto and [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source
                        text not declassified</hi>] matters on a low key and while we should take
                    such actions as are necessary to “keep our hand in,” and to keep these
                    characters from accepting help from Moscow and Peiping, and hence become their
                    instruments, nevertheless this was not the time to develop the Congo and
                    exacerbate the situation in Angola and [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line
                        of source text not declassified</hi>].</p>
                <p>[Here follows discussion of other subjects.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d425-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d425-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Central Intelligence Agency, DCI (McCone) Files: Job 80–B01285A, 303 Committee Meetings, 1964.
                    Secret; Eyes Only. Drafted by McCone on
                    August 8.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d425-f2" n="2" xml:id="d425-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to a CIA paper, “Covert Support for
                    Selected Angolan Nationalist Leaders,” dated August 3, which requested authority
                    to provide covert support to selected Angolan nationalist leaders [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]. (Department of State,
                        INR/IL Historical Files, 303 Committee
                    Files, 303 C. 7, August 6, 1964)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d425-f3" n="3" xml:id="d425-f3-content">
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
